WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.313
An employee with potential.

2
00:00:03.363 --> 00:00:05.834
A next step that presents itself.

3
00:00:05.884 --> 00:00:09.807
An organisation that wants to make that choice well.

4
00:00:09.857 --> 00:00:14.171
Because talent does not come into its own by itself.

5
00:00:14.221 --> 00:00:21.473
That only happens where role, context,
energy and drivers genuinely support each other.

6
00:00:21.523 --> 00:00:26.399
That is what the Development & Mobility journey makes visible.

7
00:00:26.449 --> 00:00:33.787
Not as a loose development wish,
but as a well-founded choice about growth and employability.

8
00:00:33.837 --> 00:00:38.320
The starting point is the individual profile.

9
00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:52.120
Talent pattern, drivers, energy and development direction make visible
where potential is supported, and where the context holds it back.

10
00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:55.786
That is how it becomes clear which step fits.

11
00:00:55.836 --> 00:01:07.435
Deepening in the current role, broadening into a different context,
or developing in a focused way towards a next move within the organisation.

12
00:01:07.485 --> 00:01:10.235
That makes the conversation concrete.

13
00:01:10.285 --> 00:01:19.845
Not only about ambition, but also about feasibility, timing,
guidance and the setting that makes durable contribution possible.

14
00:01:19.895 --> 00:01:33.107
For HR, internal coaches and managers, this creates a stronger picture of how the
talents already present can truly be unlocked, instead of unknowingly held back.

15
00:01:33.907 --> 00:01:36.241
No promise of success.

16
00:01:36.341 --> 00:01:38.472
No automatic progression.

17
00:01:38.572 --> 00:01:42.908
The decision stays with people and the organisation.

